# Inventory rows Q2 to Q6 classified against Pekko v1.7.1 (audit #004, block 5, 2026-10-27)

**Status: documentation only.** This classifies the pending rows Q2 to Q6 of the #1208 inventories (`INV-A`, `INV-T`). It implements nothing, accepts no
decision, and changes no issue, label, state or ADR status. Every "Proposed action" and every Owner question is a proposal.

- **Accepted authority.** Only [ADR 0033](../adr/0033-actor-typed-scope-and-architecture.md) (accepted 2026-10-24, D1 to D13). ADR 0034 and ADR 0035 are **proposed**; nothing below relies on them.
- **Closed exclusion vocabulary.** The seven codes (`jvm-only`, `java-api`, `replaced-by-go-stdlib`, `replaced-by-goPekko-module`, `cluster-or-remote`, `network-io`, `owner-excluded`) are in `docs/actor-typed-completion-design.md:342`, **not** in accepted ADR text (ADR 0033 D13 says only "agreed local frontier and documented JVM-only APIs"). No code was invented; The bodies of #1072, #1074, #1079, #1081, #1084, #1086 and #1044 R1 attribute this list to ADR 0033 D13; accepted text does not support that attribution. Where none fits, the row says so and the question goes to the Owner.
- **Evidence levels.** "Spec read" means a Pekko spec was opened; "READ" means code only. Nothing was executed: no Pekko program, no Go suite. "Spec not located" is not "no oracle" (ADR 0033 D13).

