## 8. Reconciliation 2026-10-27: canonical row set and counts

This PR is the canonical classification of Q2 to Q6. PR #1216 (closed as a duplicate) classified the same rows; its corrections that
held were folded into the rows above on 2026-10-27, and its counts are reconciled here.

**Universe (88).** Rule: a table row of `inventory/INV-A-actor.md` or `inventory/INV-T-typed.md` at #1208 head `80a691279e` whose `Scope`
(INV-A) or `Scope class` (INV-T) cell starts with `uncl`. Result: INV-A 67, INV-T 21. By table shape: 82 rows in capability tables,
4 `reference.conf` key-group rows (INV-A lines 288, 292, 293, 297) and 2 rows of the INV-T Java table (lines 188, 189).

**86 versus 88.** Block 1 reported 86 with a parser that is not kept. 88 minus the two INV-T Java-table rows is 86, and INV-T's own
summary counts 19 of its 21 rows, leaving out the same two. The explanation is consistent but not proven; 88 is the canonical
denominator because it follows from a stated rule.

**81 versus 79.** Both start from the same 88. This PR puts 7 rows in Q1 (INV-T 45, 50, 57, 73, 118, 119, 121) and classifies 81. #1216
also put INV-T 99 (Typed context thread guard) and INV-A 78 (`ClassicActorSystemProvider`) in Q1 and classified 79. Canonical: **81**,
with T99 in Q2 and A78 in Q6, because both rows are classified here and Q1 is out of scope. Eighteen rows carry a different group
label in #1216 (A128, A173, A211, A234 in Q3 or Q2; A142, A58, A77, A292, A293, A297 in Q5; A144, A229, A230, A236, A239, A240, A241,
A30 in Q2 or Q6). Group labels are the Architect's reading and do not change any row's classification; this PR's labels are canonical.

**Exclusions.** #1216 counted the Java serializers (A211) as excluded by ADR 0021. That is wrong: ADR 0021 mentions Java serialization
only at line 331, inside "Upstream cases planned to be ported", in the same sentence as the pending O7. Both PRs agree that the async
DNS socket client (A263) falls under ADR 0033 D8; it is recorded above as excluded by accepted category with the per-item record
pending. Canonical: 1 row excluded by an accepted category, 34 exclusion-proposed, 12 included (behavior), 34 pending (section 3).

**#1085.** #1216 said #1085 does not list `system-shutdown-default` and `throw-on-shutdown-timeout`; the issue body lists all seven
testkit keys (body line 94). This PR's Q6-T223 row is right.

**Classification is not an implementation gate.** OD-1 to OD-11 decide how rows are recorded. A story is blocked only by the decisions
and contracts it actually consumes.

